Database migrations

The original phase-by-phase migration files were not included in this
checkout. The phase11_baseline revision snapshots the delivered schema;
large_email_payloads widens the MySQL email body and raw payload columns.

Fresh, empty database (PowerShell, from emailorbit/):
    $env:FLASK_APP = "run.py"
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m flask db upgrade

Existing database with the complete Phase 11 schema and no Alembic history:
    Back up the database and verify its schema matches 0001_phase11_baseline.py.
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m flask db stamp phase11_baseline
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m flask db upgrade

Stamping records a revision; it does not create or repair any tables. Do not
stamp a database that is missing Phase 11 fields. If a database already has
an older Alembic revision, recover its original migration files and reconcile
the histories before using this replacement baseline.

Future schema changes use flask db migrate, followed by flask db upgrade.
Do not run the historical README's phase-by-phase init/migrate commands on
top of this migration directory. Downgrading LONGTEXT can lose oversized data;
check stored lengths before downgrading.
